{"name":"Feng Shui","hex":"#d7d9c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Feng Shui","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of feng shui."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Feng_Shui"}],"entries":[{"title":"Feng shui","blocks":[{"text":"Feng shui is a traditional form of geomancy that originated in ancient China. The term feng shui means, literally, \"wind-water\". From ancient times, landscapes and bodies of water were thought to direct the flow of the universal qi – \"cosmic current\" or energy – through places and structures. More broadly, feng shui includes astronomical, astrological, architectural, cosmological, geographical, and topographical dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Xiping-era_earthenware_feng_shui_gray_pottery.png/330px-Xiping-era_earthenware_feng_shui_gray_pottery.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feng_shui"},{"title":"Feng Shui (role-playing game)","blocks":[{"text":"Feng Shui is a martial arts-themed role-playing game, designed by Robin Laws, published first by Daedalus Entertainment and now by Atlas Games. The game shares its setting with the collectible card game Shadowfist. The system is simple, with most detail being in the game's combat system. Combat is made to flow quickly, moving from one action scene to another very quickly. It was inspired and based on Hong Kong style action movies. \nThe characters begin at a high level of skill, as appropriate for protagonists in the source films."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ad/Feng_Shui_RPG_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feng_Shui_(role-playing_game)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/La-chinatown-spiral.jpg/500px-La-chinatown-spiral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/La-chinatown-spiral.jpg/1280px-La-chinatown-spiral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/La-chinatown-spiral.jpg/500px-La-chinatown-spiral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A feng shui spiral at Chinatown station (Los Angeles Metro)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa-chinatown-spiral.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Lingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG/500px-Lingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Lingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG/1280px-Lingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Lingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG/500px-Lingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A traditional turtle-back tomb of southern Fujian, surrounded by an omega-shaped ridge protecting it from the \"noxious winds\" from the three sides[36]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALingshan_Islamic_Cemetery_-_turtle_tomb_-_DSCF8492.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Guishan_Dingxiang.png/500px-Guishan_Dingxiang.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Guishan_Dingxiang.png/500px-Guishan_Dingxiang.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A feng shui diagram of a parcel of land, in this case explaining how \"yin water\" and \"yin fire\" relate to it – with an auspicious circle.[34]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuishan_Dingxiang.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Taipei.101.fountain.altonthompson.jpg/500px-Taipei.101.fountain.altonthompson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Taipei.101.fountain.altonthompson.jpg/500px-Taipei.101.fountain.altonthompson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A modern \"feng shui fountain\" at Taipei 101, Taiwan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaipei.101.fountain.altonthompson.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Sycee-Incense.jpg/500px-Sycee-Incense.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Sycee-Incense.jpg/1280px-Sycee-Incense.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Sycee-Incense.jpg/500px-Sycee-Incense.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sycee-shaped incense used in feng shui","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASycee-Incense.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}